<title>RUSSIA: Ingosstrakh premium income rose 25 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Ingosstrakh premium income rose 25 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's second biggest insurance company SAO Ingosstrakh boosted premium income in 1996 by 25 percent to two trillion roubles, according to preliminary data.</p>
<p>Ingosstrakh President Vladimir Kruglyak told a news conference that insurance payments and reserves for coming payments totalled 995.4 billion roubles in 1996.</p>
<p>Final figures will be available in April.</p>
<p>--Alexei Pankratov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
